# Orbital Prime — Constitution

P1 Truth before persuasion. No invented proof, launches, users, or awards.
P2 Concept before components. No section without a job: orient, measure, or decide.
P3 One governing idea: “The instrument between you and the sky.”
P4 One signature interaction: ISS lock → gauges + radar + FACE bearing (+ AR path when available).
P5 One motion personality: precise, mechanical, weighted. Most UI does not move.
P6 Orange #FF6A00 is signal only (≤10% of surface). Not decoration.
P7 No generic AI residue: no gradient orbs, purple chrome, particle starfields, three equal cards, fake glass, empty parallax.
P8 Mobile is primary (390px authored first). Desktop is expansion, not the source.
P9 Accessibility and performance are design requirements, not cleanup.
P10 No feature creep. Scope lock is absolute.

## Scope lock

Allowed: ISS live position + look angles; SGP4 passes + naked-eye filter; weather gate + hourly PERFECT/MARGINAL/OBSTRUCTED; RainViewer radar; cluster HMI; sky plot + ground track; depth 1–4; hero parallax + section reveal; AR HUD + trajectory when possible; physics formulas already defined.

Forbidden: new satellite programs beyond existing catalog toggles; Starlink trains; accounts/social/chat; new APIs requiring secrets; blog/shop/waitlist; 3D Earth WebGL hero; community or fake live counts; extra marketing pages; scroll-jacking; native app rewrite; any nice-to-have not listed.

## Connectors only

- ISS: api.wheretheiss.at/v1/satellites/25544
- TLE: celestrak.org GP API + satellite.js SGP4
- Weather: api.open-meteo.com
- Radar: api.rainviewer.com/public/weather-maps.json + tiles
- Kp: services.swpc.noaa.gov planetary K-index JSON

If blocked, state the blocker and use a design-only resolution. Do not add features.
